title: The Old Hermit
weight: 10
cooldown: 0
---

=== intro

The old hermit sits cross-legged on a moss-covered stone, his white beard nearly touching the ground. As you approach, his eyes - ancient and knowing - fix upon you with unsettling intensity.

"Another seeker," he rasps. "They come more frequently now. The darkness stirs in the ruins, and it calls to the curious and the foolish alike."

He gestures for you to sit. "Tell me, traveler - why do you walk this path?"

* [I seek adventure and treasure]
  -> treasure_seeker

* [I want to stop whatever evil lurks in the ruins]
  -> hero_path

* [I'm just exploring] { !flag.hermit_tested }
  -> explorer

* [I've learned about the dangers and come prepared] { flag.knows_about_undead }
  -> prepared

=== treasure_seeker

The hermit sighs, a sound like wind through dead leaves. "Gold and glory. The ruins have claimed many who sought such things." His eyes bore into yours. "But I sense something more in you. A spark of curiosity, perhaps even compassion."

"Tell me true - if you found someone in need within those walls, would you help them? Even at cost to yourself?"

* [Of course I would help]
  -> test_passed

* [It depends on the situation]
  -> test_failed

* [My survival comes first]
  -> test_failed

=== hero_path

A faint smile crosses the hermit's weathered face. "A noble answer. But nobility is easily spoken. Let me tell you what waits in those ruins."

"Long ago, this was a temple. Holy men lived there, seeking wisdom. But they delved too deep into forbidden knowledge, and something answered their call. Something that should have remained sleeping."

"Now their spirits are bound there, trapped between life and death. They suffer endlessly." He pauses. "Can you face such horror? Can you offer them peace?"

* [I will try]
  -> test_passed

* [How would I give them peace?]
  -> peace_method

* [Perhaps I'm not ready]
  -> not_ready

=== explorer

The hermit shakes his head slowly. "The curious are the most dangerous of all. Curiosity without purpose, without respect for what lies beyond." He stands, surprisingly spry for his apparent age.

"Come back when you understand what you seek. The ruins are not for idle wandering."

~ damage 5

* [I'll return when I'm ready]
  -> END

=== prepared

The hermit's eyes widen slightly. "You've spoken to others. You know what you face." He nods approvingly. "Silver against the corrupted spirits. Light to pierce their darkness. And courage to face what was once human."

"You may pass. But remember - the key to the inner chamber lies in the tavern's cellar. Without it, you cannot reach the heart of evil."

~ set_flag "hermit_approved"
~ heal 10

* [Thank you for your wisdom]
  -> farewell_approved

=== peace_method

"There is an artifact within - an ancient scroll of unbinding. With it, you can release the trapped souls. But the scroll is guarded by the most corrupted spirit of all: the High Priest who first made the bargain."

The hermit places a hand on your shoulder. "If you can defeat him and read the scroll, you will free them all. Are you willing?"

* [I am willing]
  -> test_passed

* [I need to think about this]
  -> not_ready

=== test_passed

The hermit rises and places a weathered hand on your head. You feel a warmth spread through you - ancient magic, protective and kind.

"You may pass, seeker. The path to the ruins lies north from here. But heed my words: take the old key from the tavern cellar. Without it, the inner sanctum remains sealed."

~ set_flag "hermit_approved"
~ heal 25

* [Thank you, wise one]
  -> farewell_approved

=== test_failed

The hermit's expression hardens. "Your heart is not yet ready for this burden. Go back to the village. Speak to Grenda and Aldric. Learn the stories. Understand what was lost here."

He waves his hand dismissively. "Return when you have grown."

~ damage 10

* [I understand]
  -> END

=== not_ready

The hermit nods sagely. "Wisdom is knowing your limits. Go, prepare yourself. Speak to others, gather what you need. The ruins have waited centuries - they can wait a little longer."

* [I will return]
  -> END

=== farewell_approved

The hermit bows his head. "May the light guide your steps, and may you bring peace to the suffering souls within."

He settles back onto his stone, closing his eyes. "The path awaits. Go now, while your courage is fresh."

-> END
